NAME
       pvdisplay - show the details of physical volumes

SYNOPSIS
       pvdisplay [-m] [-s] [-C] [PV...]

DESCRIPTION
       pvdisplay prints a block of details for each physical volume: device
       name, volume group, size, the size of one extent (PE Size), the number
       of extents in total, free and allocated, and the UUID. With no PV
       names it shows them all.

OPTIONS
       -m, --maps
              Also show which extents belong to which logical volume.

       -s, --short
              One short line per PV.

       -C, --columns
              Print a table, like pvs.

EXAMPLES
           pvdisplay /dev/vdb1
           pvdisplay -m /dev/vdc

SEE ALSO
       pvs(8), vgdisplay(8), lvdisplay(8), lvm(8)
